-- title:
--   Finite spanning set over the descended node ring at level two
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$, let $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ be a ring homomorphism, let $a \in k$, and let $K$ be a number field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, i.e.\ an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ finite over $\mathbb Q$. Write $A_K = A \cap K$ (the subring `coeffSubring A K`), let $\mathrm{red}_K$ be the restriction of $\mathrm{red}$ to $A_K$, and let $R_0 =$ `modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) ...` be the subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}(\!(\mathsf q)\!)$ consisting of those Laurent series $f$ for which there are two-variable polynomials $r, s$ over $A_K$ with $s$ not vanishing at $(a, a^q)$ under the evaluation through $\mathrm{red}_K$, and $f \cdot s(j, j_{q}) = r(j, j_{q})$, where $j =$ `jqModC` and $j_q =$ `jqNModC` at level $1 \cdot q$; assume $R_0$ is Noetherian. Let $\varphi =$ `qExpand _ 2` be the doubling of exponents, let $L =$ `lambdaFieldOver q K` be the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $\lambda$ and its $q$-fold re-expansion $\lambda_q$, and let $F =$ `fieldOver (1 * q) K` be the subfield generated by the constant series from $K$ together with $j$ and $j_q$. Then there is a finite set $t$ of Laurent series such that every $c \in t$ lies in $L$ and is integral over the image $\varphi(R_0)$, and such that every $x \in L$ integral over $\varphi(R_0)$ can be written as $x = \sum_{c \in t} f(c)\, c$ for some function $f$ on Laurent series whose values $f(c)$, for $c \in t$, lie in $\varphi(F)$ and are integral over $\varphi(R_0)$.
--
--   This is the finiteness of the integral closure of the localised node ring, transported to level two: the elements of the $\lambda$-field $L$ integral over $\varphi(R_0)$ are spanned by finitely many elements over the elements of $\varphi(F)$ integral over $\varphi(R_0)$, stated in instance-free spanning-set form. It is used to establish module-finiteness of that integral closure in [`ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.moduleFinite_of_forall_mem_iff_isIntegralElem_qExpand_modularLocalizedAtPoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LambdaNodeLocalized.moduleFinite_of_forall_mem_iff_isIntegralElem_qExpand_modularLocalizedAtPoint).
